    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0225" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg183"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 357.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 27, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit copies of two
                    notes, dated the 21st and 23d of this month, which have passed between Lord
                    Russell and myself, respecting <pb facs="0226" n="184" xml:id="pg184"/> certain
                    operations of the rebels in fitting out an armed vessel at Glasgow. It is proper
                    to mention that the investigation appears to have been initiated by his lordship
                    upon information not furnished from this legation, and that his communication to
                    me was perfectly spontaneous.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d133-a1.xml" xpointer="d133-a1"/>
